  mutates a task outside a request.

  [1mFrontend.[0m I'd suggest a small React + TypeScript SPA built with Vite, replacing the current [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. It's
  conventional, and notifications will eventually want live updates, which is markedly easier with a component model
  than with hand-rolled DOM updates. This is the most reversible decision in the design — the API doesn't care — so I'm
  not going to argue hard for it.

  [1mTooling[0m — cheapest to establish now, before any code exists. My proposal:

  - [1mLinting + formatting:[0m ruff (lint + format) for Python, ESLint + Prettier for the frontend. Your [38;5;153mCLAUDE.md[39m already
    standardizes on ruff.
  - [1mType checking:[0m mypy on the Python side, [38;5;153mtsc --noEmit[39m on the frontend. Also per your conventions.
  - [1mUnit tests:[0m pytest with a real Postgres in a container, transaction-rollback fixtures per test. Testing against
    SQLite and deploying on Postgres is a well-known way to discover dialect differences in production.
  - [1mE2E tests:[0m Playwright against a running stack. Worth it here because auth flows are exactly what unit tests miss.
  - [1mDependencies:[0m uv, project-local [38;5;153m.venv[39m, per your documented rule about never polluting the global env.

  These land in the spec's Global Constraints so every later plan inherits them.

  I left out CI config, containerization, and migrations-on-deploy — all reasonable, none of which need deciding before
  there's code to run.
